// expect: E0729
// Example 33 — Wrong sanitizer at a boundary (iter 51, BUGS.md BUG-023).
//
// Aether's sanitizers are SINK-specific, and the diagnostics say so:
// E0725's own hint ends "(sanitizeLog does NOT protect here)". Written
// inline, `htmlResponse(sanitizeLog(u))` has always been refused.
//
// The boundary rule E0729 was coarser than the sink rules it protects.
// `boundary_markers()` unions every Untrusted row's sanitizer into ONE
// set — {sanitizeLog, htmlEscape, sanitizeHeader, csvEscape, trusted} —
// and any member of it cleared the crossing, whatever the callee went on
// to do with the value. So moving the sink one call away laundered it:
// `render(sanitizeLog(u))` was exit 0 while `render` fed the same value
// straight into `htmlResponse`.
//
// E0729 now summarises which sinks each callee parameter reaches and
// demands the sanitizer THAT sink asks for. Stripping CR/LF does nothing
// about `<script>`.
//
// The fix: `render(htmlEscape(u))`, or type the parameter
// `s: Untrusted<String>` so the marker travels and E0725 judges the sink
// in place.

function render(s: String) returns String
  effects pure
do
  return htmlResponse(s)
end

function handle(u: Untrusted<String>) returns String
  effects pure
do
  // E0729: cleared with sanitizeLog(...), but render passes it to
  // 'htmlResponse', whose sanitizer is htmlEscape.
  return render(sanitizeLog(u))
end
